  "version": 1,
  "title": "Conditional ZF-independence of the exact 192-state machine",
  "abstract": "A binary 192-state machine with a contextual scanner that, under consistency of first-order ZF, runs forever and has no ZF proof of its nonhalting. Arithmetic Sigma-1 soundness implies unprovability in both directions. The halting sentence expresses the literal machine's behavior in every ZF model.",
